\f6\b\fs36 \cf0 1.3 ExecutionGraph schema (deep)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs32 \cf0 We want a graph that is simple enough to implement, but expressive enough to be a real control plane.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 1.3.1 Top-level ExecutionGraph\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f12\b0\fs28 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \cb13 ExecutionGraph \{\
  "id": "string",                 // e.g. "demo_multiagent_v1"\
  "name": "string",               // human-readable\
  "version": "string",            // e.g. "1.0.0"\
  "description": "string",        // optional\
  "steps": [ExecutionGraphStep]   // ordered list for v1\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs32 \cf0 \cb1 v1 can be linear in execution order; later you can add explicit dependencies and topological sort.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 1.3.2 ExecutionGraphStep\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f12\b0\fs28 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \cb13 ExecutionGraphStep \{\
  "id": "string",                // unique within graph\
  "kind": "string",              // one of \{ "transform", "fanout", "metric", "decision", "persist", "tool_call", "info" \}\
  "description": "string",       // short human description\
\
  "inputs": ["string"],          // names of context keys to read\
  "outputs": ["string"],         // names of context keys to write\
\
  "agents": ["string"],          // optional, for fanout or multi-agent decision\
  "tool_name": "string|null",    // optional, for tool_call\
  "params": \{                    // free-form config for step\
    // e.g. thresholds, flags, etc.\
  \}\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs32 \cf0 \cb1 We constrain 
\f8\fs28 \cb12 kind
\f0\fs32 \cb1  to a small vocabulary so the engine/explainer can know what\'92s going on:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls335\ilvl0
\f8\fs28 \cf0 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
transform
\f0\fs32 \cb1 : pure data transformation.\
\ls335\ilvl0
\f8\fs28 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
fanout
\f0\fs32 \cb1 : run multiple agents given some input.\
\ls335\ilvl0
\f8\fs28 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
metric
\f0\fs32 \cb1 : compute numeric metrics on context data (e.g. disagreement).\
\ls335\ilvl0
\f8\fs28 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
decision
\f0\fs32 \cb1 : choose an answer/label, maybe using metrics.\
\ls335\ilvl0
\f8\fs28 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
persist
\f0\fs32 \cb1 : build/store Episode and its ID.\
\ls335\ilvl0
\f8\fs28 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
tool_call
\f0\fs32 \cb1 : call external tool, write results.\
\ls335\ilvl0
\f8\fs28 \cb12 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
info
\f0\fs32 \cb1 : bookkeeping; emit events without changing context.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0
\cf0 In v1, you can guarantee linear order by executing 
\f8\fs28 \cb12 steps
\f0\fs32 \cb1  in listed order. Later, we can add 
\f8\fs28 \cb12 depends_on
\f0\fs32 \cb1  for more complex graphs.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
