## 2. Problem and Motivation\
\
### 2.1 Fragmented Multi-Model Systems\
\
\cf17 -\cf0  Describe how real systems (LLMs + tools, autonomy stacks, diagnostic systems) are collections of models and services glued together ad-hoc.\
\cf17 -\cf0  Explain that logs are text, not structured episodes.\
\
### 2.2 Wasted Model Disagreement\
\
\cf17 -\cf0  Note that many groups already run multiple models/agents but do not systematically log and use disagreement as a training signal.\
\cf17 -\cf0  Mention issues: edge cases disappear into logs; hard scenarios not surfaced.\
\
### 2.3 Lack of Replayable Decision Records\
\
\cf17 -\cf0  Outline the difficulty of answering "what happened" in a way that is:\
\cf17   -\cf0  machine-readable,\
\cf17   -\cf0  replayable,\
\cf17   -\cf0  auditable.\
\
### 2.4 Ad-Hoc Orchestration Glue\
\
\cf17 -\cf0  Each team writes custom scripts / chains with no standard representation.\
\cf17 -\cf0  This blocks reuse, analysis, and cross-system comparison.\
\
