## 3. Proposed Innovation: GhostLink Primitives\
\
Here you define the core **objects**.\
\
### 3.1 Agent\
\
\cf17 -\cf0  Logical participant (model or tool).\
\cf17 -\cf0  Fields: `name`, `version`, `role`, `kind`, `config`.\
\
### 3.2 Episode\
\
\cf17 -\cf0  Canonical record of one run:\
\cf17   -\cf0  `input` (task),\
\cf17   -\cf0  `agents`,\
\cf17   -\cf0  `outputs`,\
\cf17   -\cf0  `disagreement`,\
\cf17   -\cf0  `tools_invoked`,\
\cf17   -\cf0  `final_decision`,\
\cf17   -\cf0  `metadata`.\
\cf17 -\cf0  State invariant: all agent outputs in one Episode share the same input.\
\
### 3.3 ExecutionGraph\
\
\cf17 -\cf0  Declarative procedure:\
\cf17   -\cf0  Steps: `transform`, `fanout`, `metric`, `decision`, `persist`, `tool_call`.\
\cf17 -\cf0  Encodes how Episodes are produced.\
\
### 3.4 TraceEvent\
\
\cf17 -\cf0  Runtime evidence: what each step did and in what order.\
\cf17 -\cf0  Used for inspection, debugging, and audit.\
\
### 3.5 Backend Service\
\
\cf17 -\cf0  Simple API for storing and retrieving Episodes.\
\cf17 -\cf0  Designed to integrate with training/eval stacks.\
\
### 3.6 Explainer Agent\
\
\cf17 -\cf0  Meta-LLM that consumes `\{graph, trace, episode\}` and produces a structured `Explanation` for humans.\
\
