## 7. Risks and Mitigations\
\
\cf17 -\cf0  **Complexity Creep**\
\cf17   -\cf0  Risk: schema + graphs become too complex.\
\cf17   -\cf0  Mitigation: narrow v1 to a single canonical pipeline and minimal schema.\
\cf17 -\cf0  **External Dependency Drift**\
\cf17   -\cf0  Risk: model APIs/tools change.\
\cf17   -\cf0  Mitigation: thin Agent interface, explicit versioning.\
\cf17 -\cf0  **Schema Instability**\
\cf17   -\cf0  Risk: changes break Episodes.\
\cf17   -\cf0  Mitigation: `schema_version`, migration strategy.\
\cf17 -\cf0  **Explainer Accuracy**\
\cf17   -\cf0  Risk: explainer agent mis-describes runs.\
\cf17   -\cf0  Mitigation: require explanations to reference step IDs, trace data.\
