  \cf14 date:\cf0  \cf15 "2025-11-26"\cf0 \
  \cf14 keywords:\cf0 \
    \cf17 -\cf0  \cf15 "multi-agent orchestration"\cf0 \
    \cf17 -\cf0  \cf15 "emergency vehicles"\cf0 \
    \cf17 -\cf0  \cf15 "diagnostics"\cf0 \
    \cf17 -\cf0  \cf15 "training data"\cf0 \
    \cf17 -\cf0  \cf15 "GhostLink"\cf0 \
\
\cf14 sections:\cf0 \
  \cf17 -\cf0  \cf14 title:\cf0  \cf15 "Executive Summary"\cf0 \
    \cf14 blocks:\cf0 \
      \cf17 -\cf0  \cf14 type:\cf0  \cf15 "paragraph"\cf0 \
        \cf14 text:\cf0  \cf15 >\
          GhostLink is a synchronization and training OS for heterogeneous AI systems.\
          This whiteletter presents its first vertical: an Emergency Vehicle Systems Designer\
          that captures upfit design, diagnostics, and fault management as structured Episodes.\
\cf0 \
  \cf17 -\cf0  \cf14 title:\cf0  \cf15 "Problem and Motivation"\cf0 \
    \cf14 blocks:\cf0 \
      \cf17 -\cf0  \cf14 type:\cf0  \cf15 "paragraph"\cf0 \
        \cf14 text:\cf0  \cf15 >\
          Modern emergency vehicle upfits are complex high-current, high-criticality electrical systems,\
          typically designed and serviced from tacit technician knowledge and vendor-specific conventions.\
          Logs, if any, are unstructured and not reusable for training diagnostic or design agents.\
\cf0       \cf17 -\cf0  \cf14 type:\cf0  \cf15 "bullet_list"\cf0 \
        \cf14 items:\cf0 \
          \cf17 -\cf0  \cf15 "No canonical schema for vehicle platform, circuits, grounds, and control logic."\cf0 \
          \cf17 -\cf0  \cf15 "Diagnostics are performed from memory; reasoning is rarely captured."\cf0 \
          \cf17 -\cf0  \cf15 "Edge-case faults and intermittent failures are not systematically turned into training data."\cf0 \
\
  \cf17 -\cf0  \cf14 title:\cf0  \cf15 "Proposed Innovation: GhostLink Primitives"\cf0 \
    \cf14 subsections:\cf0 \
      \cf17 -\cf0  \cf14 title:\cf0  \cf15 "Episodes for Design and Diagnostics"\cf0 \
        \cf14 blocks:\cf0 \
          \cf17 -\cf0  \cf14 type:\cf0  \cf15 "paragraph"\cf0 \
            \cf14 text:\cf0  \cf15 >\
              GhostLink introduces Episodes as the canonical record for both design sessions and\
              diagnostic cases. Each Episode ties together inputs, intermediate reasoning, agent outputs,\
              disagreement metrics, and final decisions into a replayable data structure.\
\cf0       \cf17 -\cf0  \cf14 title:\cf0  \cf15 "ExecutionGraphs as Orchestration Contracts"\cf0 \
        \cf14 blocks:\cf0 \
          \cf17 -\cf0  \cf14 type:\cf0  \cf15 "paragraph"\cf0 \
            \cf14 text:\cf0  \cf15 >\
              ExecutionGraphs define the ordered steps used to synthesize a vehicle design or walk\
              a technician through a diagnostic flow. They are explicit contracts between the system\
              and its operators.\
\cf0 \
  \cf17 -\cf0  \cf14 title:\cf0  \cf15 "Emergency Vehicle Systems Designer"\cf0 \
    \cf14 blocks:\cf0 \
      \cf17 -\cf0  \cf14 type:\cf0  \cf15 "paragraph"\cf0 \
        \cf14 text:\cf0  \cf15 >\
          The Emergency Vehicle Systems Designer is a GhostLink-based application that turns platform\
          specifications, load inventories, and operating constraints into a structured design. The same\
          substrate encodes diagnostic flows and captures real-world troubleshooting as Episodes.\
\cf0 \
  \cf17 -\cf0  \cf14 title:\cf0  \cf15 "Evaluation and Future Work"\cf0 \
    \cf14 blocks:\cf0 \
      \cf17 -\cf0  \cf14 type:\cf0  \cf15 "bullet_list"\cf0 \
        \cf14 items:\cf0 \
          \cf17 -\cf0  \cf15 "Measure design consistency and fault rate across rigs built from the tool."\cf0 \
          \cf17 -\cf0  \cf15 "Train diagnostic agents on captured Episodes from real vehicles."\cf0 \
          \cf17 -\cf0  \cf15 "Generalize the approach to other safety-critical platforms."\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa80\partightenfactor0

