==================================================\
CONCEPTUAL NORTH STAR\
==================================================\
\
GhostLink is a **synchronization and training OS** for heterogeneous AI systems.\
\
Key ideas:\
\
1. **Episodes as canonical records**  \
   Every \'93run\'94 (design session, diagnostic session, reasoning task, etc.) is captured as a structured **Episode**. An Episode ties together:\
   - input task,\
   - agents involved,\
   - their outputs,\
   - explicit disagreement metrics,\
   - the final decision,\
   - and metadata (versions, tags, provenance).\
\
2. **ExecutionGraphs as orchestration contracts**  \
   How an Episode is *produced* is defined by an **ExecutionGraph**: an ordered set of steps (transform, fanout, metric, decision, persist, tool_call, info) that operate over a shared context.\
\
3. **TraceEvents as causal evidence**  \
   Each run also emits a sequence of **TraceEvents**, which record what each step did, in what order, with what intermediate data. This is for inspection, audit, and debugging.\
\
4. **Disagreement as signal**  \
   GhostLink is built to run multiple agents/models/tools on the same input, compute disagreement between their outputs, and use that as:\
   - a routing signal (when to escalate / ask for tools / human review),\
   - a data-engine signal (which Episodes to use for training/eval).\
\
5. **Closed loop with training**  \
   Episodes are later turned into:\
   - supervised training rows (input \uc0\u8594  final_decision),\
   - preference data (final_decision vs alternatives),\
   - reward model training data,\
   - evaluation sets (especially for high-disagreement cases).\
\
GhostLink is NOT a \'93demo framework\'94. It\'92s a **data & orchestration substrate** meant to ground in hard, real domains starting with **emergency vehicles** and eventually extending to autonomy, truth-seeking systems, etc.\
\
==================================================\
LANGUAGE, STACK, GENERAL RULES\
==================================================\
\
- Primary language: **Python 3.10+**.\
- Use **type hints** everywhere.\
- Prefer:\
  - `dataclasses` or Pydantic models for schemas,\
  - clear module boundaries over giant files,\
  - small, testable functions.\
- Avoid framework lock-in unless explicitly asked.\
- No unnecessary cleverness; explicit > magical.\
\
When unsure:\
- Extend existing patterns (Episode, ExecutionGraph, Trace, domain models).\
- Keep code predictable and inspectable.\
- Think in terms of \'93can I serialize this to JSON / YAML and use it later?\'94.\
